│ of atracurium to antagonism of neuromuscular block [29 (2) vs 53 (9) min, P<0.005] and from antagonism to extubation │
│ [6 (1) vs 15 (4) min, P<0.01]. Duration of surgical procedure was the sole multivariate predictor of PORC [odds      │
│ ratio 0.94 (95% confidence intervals 0.91–0.98), P<0.01].                    Conclusions. PORC remains a clinical    │
│ problem despite use of intermediate‐duration neuromuscular blocking drugs and peripheral nerve stimulators. Patients │
│ undergoing procedures of short duration may be at risk of inappropriately early tracheal extubation, possibly due to │
│ work pressures. The association between suboptimal antagonism of neuromuscular blockade and short procedures needs   │
